# Mandatory shadcn Patterns

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: L0 rule router for shadcn work.

## Use This When

- Start here for any shadcn component, styling, form, composition, icon, registry, or CLI request.

## Stop Here If

- Stop after selecting one or two focused shadcn references.
- Do not keep the full shadcn pack loaded when only one rule leaf is needed.

## Descend To

- Skill router: `/.agents/skills/shadcn/SKILL.md`
- React bridge: `/.cursor/rules/shadcn-patterns-react-ui.mdc`
- Continue within this file for mandatory loading behavior and project-wide enforcement.

Use the shadcn patterns below as required project conventions, not optional suggestions.

## Exception — `apps/author` admin

The `apps/author` Payload admin panel uses Payload's own component library (`@payloadcms/ui`) for its admin views — it consolidates on one design system inside the Payload admin runtime. shadcn (`@workspace/ui`) stays mandatory for every other surface: `apps/platform`, `apps/web`, and any end-user-facing pages (including a future end-user authoring surface, should one exist). Do not convert author admin views to shadcn.

Reference sources:
- `/.agents/skills/shadcn/rules/`
- `/.agents/skills/shadcn/SKILL.md`
- `/.agents/skills/shadcn/cli.md`
- `/.agents/skills/shadcn/customization.md`

## Mandatory context loading

For any request that touches shadcn UI (new component, visual refactor, styling, composition, forms, icons, or CLI updates), first load the shadcn skill pack context from:

- `/.agents/skills/shadcn/SKILL.md`
- all files in `/.agents/skills/shadcn/rules/`
- `/.agents/skills/shadcn/cli.md`
- `/.agents/skills/shadcn/customization.md`

Do not rely on memory-only assumptions when these references are available.

## Forms and fields

- Always structure forms with `FieldGroup` + `Field`.
- Use `FieldLabel` and `FieldDescription` for label/help text.
- Use `FieldSet` + `FieldLegend` for grouped options.
- Do not use raw `div` stacks as a replacement for `FieldGroup`/`Field`.

## Inputs and composition

- Use the standardized UI components from `@workspace/ui/components/*`.
- Use `Textarea` for multiline input (not raw `<textarea>`).
- Inside `InputGroup`, only use `InputGroupInput` / `InputGroupTextarea`.
- For action buttons attached to input controls, use `InputGroupAddon` (no ad-hoc absolute positioning).

## State and accessibility

- For invalid/disabled controls, apply both container and control states:
  - container: `data-invalid` / `data-disabled` on `Field`
  - control: `aria-invalid` / `disabled` on the input control

## Global shadcn checks (not forms-only)

- Prefer existing shadcn components over custom markup.
- Use semantic tokens and variants instead of raw color utility overrides.
- Use `gap-*` in flex/grid layouts, avoid `space-x-*` / `space-y-*`.
- Follow composition constraints from shadcn rules (groups, titles, required subcomponents).
- Follow icon rules (`data-icon`, no forced icon sizing in component children).

## New form default

- For new interactive forms, default to TanStack Form + schema validation.
- Follow shadcn TanStack form pattern (`Field`, `FieldGroup`, `FieldError`, `data-invalid`, `aria-invalid`).
- Prefer shared TanStack re-export from `@workspace/ui/components/tanstack-form`.
- If a form intentionally does not use TanStack Form, document the reason in task notes.

If there is a conflict between existing code and these rules, prefer refactoring toward these patterns.
